Wow. I was just thinking about that - Pimsleur Lojban. I've used Pimsleur to
some success in French, but found that the overall method for inducing
speech memory was tremendously useful.

I would be a huge fan of supporting an effort to get a basic working
vocabulary established through a program like this.

Imagine: people would download mp3's that would take them through
conversations in lojban, starting with introductory lessons and progressing
to more advanced sentence construction techniques.

This might be a fast, efficient way to tap the iPod fanbase, and to pull in
hundreds of new active speakers.
 

 

